     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity goes up substantially, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nIf you want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
